<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44413" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĭnŭessa</span></b> , ae,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a colony of the Latins</i>, <i>formerly called
				Sinope</i>, <i>in Campania</i>, now ruins near
				<i>Monte Dragone</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 4,
			9</span></i>. <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 9, § 59</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 10,
				21, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 9, 15</span></i>, A, 6; 9, 16, 1;
				<i><span class="en">Ov.
				M. 15, 715</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĭnŭessuānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Sinuessa</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deversoriolum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 12, 20</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 14, 8, 1</span></i>.—<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mansi in Sinuessano,</span>”
				<i>the Sinuessan estate</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 15, 1</span></i>
			, B, 1: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					31, 2, 4, § 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 2,
					93, 94, § 208</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 11, 7, 12</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">13, 11, 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Petrinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 5, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
